+# Successful successor with native uncertainty
+
+This optional one-shot bridge handles only `impact-initial-pass-2`, round1,
+lane3 after genuine initial all-owner reporting recovery. A successful dispatch
+with an honest uncertain review is still rejected by ordinary collection. Do
+not retry a successful immutable lane, change its report, reuse a new-context
+pack, reset counters or claim the uncertainty is resolved to unlock scheduling.
+
+Admission requires the actual paused/drained5.2 owner hold, exact current
+progress `[impact-initial, impact-initial-pass-2]`, all three successful immutable
+native successor executions and exactly one uncertain lane3 review. It binds
+actual attempt/result/prompt/final bytes and the existing persistent reporting
+home/session. Initial recovery provenance and all original duties remain owed.
+The sole native uncertainty may be deferred for scheduling; every other field
+is checked independently, including malformed fields in that uncertain row.
+
+A genuine completed root mathematical repair must exist before preview or
+record. Mechanical hashes do not establish mathematical truth. In particular,
+the machine-learning raw-filtration localization uncertainty must remain blocked
+until its original rich clause has actually been proved; a narrower statement
+is not an admission path. This adapter currently permits proof-only repair:
+Statement/Definition and frontmatter bytes must remain unchanged. The same
+repair owner supplies proof dispositions for the supplier and every current
+transitive dependency/reference consumer, even where consumer source/context
+hashes remain unchanged. Scope is derived from actual inventory. It must remain
+inside the frontier and cannot conflict with another genuine original reviewer.
+Any unsupported scope fails closed rather than dropping consumers.
+
+The root repair evidence file has:
+
+- version:1, kind:`owner-completed-proof-repair`, run,
+  phase:`impact-initial-pass-2`, round:1, unit:`3`, supplier;
+- owner_identity:`/root`, repairer_identity:the actual `/root/...` repair owner,
